{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #792: declared status 'open'. Formalized: no. Let $f(n)$ be maximal such that in any $A\\subset \\mathbb{Z}$ with $\\lvert A\\rvert=n$ there exists some sum-free subset $B\\subseteq A$ with $\\lvert B\\rvert \\geq f(n)$, so that there are no solutions to\\[a+b=c\\]with $a,b,c\\in B$. Estimate $f(n)$. Current best: The best lower bound known is\\[f(n)\\geq \\frac{n}{3}+c\\log\\log n\\]for some constant $c>0$, due to Bedert \\cite{Be25b}. The best upper bound known is\\[f(n) \\leq \\frac{n}{3}+o(n),\\]due to Eberhard, Green, and Manners \\cite{EGM14}. Prize: no. Tags: additive combinatorics."},"claim_id":"vcl_d411349ddf13c4db151ecc48dbfceb3f0bbddace807bc3ee9ef2db1701a90349","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:792","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_d36dab8d834f2ff8","object_root":"sha256:e06db96c94bf0686240f8e12c949d174a9805046070f66ca4a402078ff87e306","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","titl